  "title": "button-shortcut: Button accelerator / shortcut",
  "discussedAt": "",
  "contextReady": false,
  "contextReadyReason": "",
  "summary": "Button::shortcut(char) → composed Icon(NfIcon ⌃)+Label(letter) trailing slot inside the button; Ctrl+<c> self-submit + FocusManager::deliver_accelerator. Blocked on viewnode-all-widgets (Button) + gridui-03 NerdFont.",
  "description": "Give a `Button` an explicit **accelerator** (`Ctrl+<letter>`) rendered **inside** the button as composed content, and wire it through the confirm/modal builders.\n\n## STATUS: UNBLOCKED on the Button side (2026-07-13)\nThe blocker is gone: `Button` now **composes its content from children** (commit `07d4c1a`, PR #237) — it holds an arbitrary child tree and the size variant + state color cascade into it. So the accelerator is just **another child**, exactly as the design demands. Still blocked on **NerdFont embedding** (`gridui-03`) for the glyph.\n\n## DESIGN LOCKED (user, rescued from the old root HANDOFF.md §2/§3b — do NOT relitigate)\n- **Trigger: `Ctrl+<letter>`.** Chosen because it works in **confirm AND form dialogs** — a bare letter would collide with typing in an `Input`.\n- **Rendered INSIDE the button**, as a **composed `Icon + Label`** child (the letter next to a control glyph). **NOT** hand-drawn `cx.icon`/`cx.text`, **NOT** placed adjacent to/outside the button. With the composition refactor landed, this is now natural: `.shortcut(c)` is **sugar that appends a child**, the same way `.icon(g)` prepends one.\n- **The Button self-submits on `Ctrl+<c>`**; a host helper (`FocusManager::deliver_accelerator`) routes the accelerator to the matching **non-focused** button (otherwise only the focused button could be triggered).\n- **`ModalAction.shortcut: Option<char>`**, set by the confirm builder. The **letter is semantic** — `n` = cancel/negative, `y` = confirm/positive — and must be assigned by the **caller/builder**, because a widget cannot infer that \"Cancel\" means \"No\".\n- **Glyph: NerdFont, NOT Phosphor.** `Glyph::CaretUp` (codepoint `0xe13c`) was added for this and the user judged Phosphor's caret **ugly**. It **stays in the enum** (user directive: *keep it, do not remove*) but the accelerator uses a NerdFont control glyph instead.\n\n## Work\n1. **`gridui-03` first** — embed NerdFont (`NfIcon` + curated `NfGlyph`): vendor \"Symbols Nerd Font Mono\", confirm the license, add a renderer font family/role.\n2. `Button::shortcut(char)` → appends a trailing composed child (`NfIcon(control) + Label(letter)`); the child inherits the button's state color + size variant for free (the composition foundations).\n3. `Ctrl+<c>` self-submit in `Button::event`; `FocusManager::deliver_accelerator(root, char)` to reach a non-focused button.\n4. `ModalAction.shortcut` + the confirm builder assigning `n`/`y`; `OverlayHost` passes it through when it builds the action buttons.\n5. Docs per AGENTS.md: exhaustive, **both audiences** (native builder + the `ViewNode` prop), + showcase demo.\n\n## Files\n`heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/button.rs`, `heca-grid-ui/src/focus.rs`, `heca-grid-ui/src/widgets/icon.rs` (NfIcon), `heca/src/chrome/overlay.rs` (`ModalSpec`/`ModalAction`), `heca/src/actions.rs` (confirm builder), `docs/widgets.md`, showcase.\n\n## Gates\nclippy 0; `cargo test -p heca-grid-ui -p heca`; showcase green; no `cargo fmt`; rust SKILL review; user tests before commit.",
